     },
     "instructions": "The anchor requires that logic is not copied and pasted between files or tools; shared logic lives in one place both use. Does any step, decision or design in `item.text` go against that requirement, such as: copying, pasting, vendoring or duplicating a function or parser from one tool or file into another? An item that is silent about the requirement does not go against it.",
     "type": "choice"
    },
    "relevant": {
     "type": "choice",
     "instructions": "Does `item.text` concern source code in an sc-agent crate (crates/sc-agent*, crates/decidr or another crates/ member), judge-jev, plan-anchor, or the client template both tools use? It does when the item adds, changes, copies, ports, vendors, regenerates or wires that code, including an item that says what that code calls, uses, shares or is generated from (for example 'judge-jev and plan-anchor both call the shared client', 'add a field to a struct in crates/sc-agent-records'). It does not when the item's work is only documentation, plan notes, CI or workflow configuration, tracker housekeeping or a discussion, even if it names these tools or mentions duplication.",
     "criteria": {
